## Wrapping up

The techniques here are not exotic. Bytecode compilation, deferred
initialization, precmd hooks, conditional loading, and caching. None
of them are new ideas. The key is applying them systematically:
measure, find the bottleneck, defer or eliminate it, measure again.

Again, this is just how I like to do things. Not everyone needs to write
their own syntax highlighting or prompt. But if you enjoy being in
control of every piece of your shell, it's a rewarding way to work.

